{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#143","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#143","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#143\",\"parent_revision\":\"8ca0b81c6d2d809bd0f726ab791feb4201bcb6c45062c3c349957f6bdf884e11\",\"root_revision\":\"8ca0b81c6d2d809bd0f726ab791feb4201bcb6c45062c3c349957f6bdf884e11\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nIn `.agents/skills/receiving-pr-reviews/scripts/pr_review_threads.py`, `_run_gh`'s docstring indents `timeout:` one level too deep, so it reads as a continuation of the `args:` entry rather than its own parameter. The parameter is therefore undocumented \u2014 ruff's `D417`.\\n\\nIntroduced by the `--gh-timeout-seconds` change in #119, and invisible in this repo because `pyproject.toml` excludes `.agents/skills/*` from ruff.\\n</div>\\n\\n## How It Surfaced\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFound while porting these fixes upstream (#135). `claude_skills` *does* lint `.agents/skills/`, so the same file failed `D417` there on a path this repo reports clean. Fixed in the upstream PR; needs back-porting here so the two copies do not diverge again.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Wider Point\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis is the second time the `.agents/skills/*` ruff exclusion has hidden a real defect rather than just style churn. The exclusion exists because these files are vendored and maintained upstream, and linting them here would churn on every sync \u2014 but Codex reviews them and finds genuine bugs in them, and now so does upstream's own ruff.\\n\\nWorth deciding whether vendored skills should carry review surface here at all, rather than answering it per-incident. #135 raises the same question from the other direction.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #135 \u2014 the upstream port, where this was found\\n- #119 \u2014 where the docstring regression was introduced\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2c94d21264fcbbf336a1910f0670d53fe69704dc3b33545c205bfaaca09bed7a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-obA\"}"}